<!-- What is file? -->
A file is a place on your computer where data is stored permanently.
<!-- What is File Handling? -->
File Handling is the process of creating, opening, reading, writing, updating, and deleting files using Python.
<!-- Why Do We Need File Handling? -->
Suppose you write a program like this:
name = "bob"
print(name)
When the program ends, the value of name is lost.

<!-- Advantages of File Handling -->
✅ Permanent storage
✅ Easy to read and update
✅ Share data between programs
✅ Store large amounts of information
✅ Used in almost every software application

<!-- File Handling Operations -->

Python allows you to:

Operation	Description
Create	Create a new file
Open	Open an existing file
Read	Read data from a file
Write	Write data into a file
Append	Add data to the end of a file
Update	Modify existing data
Close	Close the file
Delete	Delete the file

